The `/*@private;` / `/*@protected;` access modifiers use comment syntax
but are not ordinary comments: the style-guide schema says formatters
"must not respace, recase or separate them from :PROCEDURE"
(procedures.visibility_annotations). Records how the formatter treats
them at a procedure boundary: annotation text and its attachment to the
following :PROCEDURE.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE PublicEntry;
:RETURN DoProc("Helper");
:ENDPROC;
/*@private;
:PROCEDURE Helper;
:RETURN 1;
:ENDPROC;
/*@protected;
:PROCEDURE Shared;
:RETURN 2;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE PublicEntry;
	:RETURN DoProc("Helper");
:ENDPROC;

/*@private;
:PROCEDURE Helper;
	:RETURN 1;
:ENDPROC;

/*@protected;
:PROCEDURE Shared;
	:RETURN 2;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
4:1-4:12 info visibility_annotation_usage: Visibility annotation '/*@private;' - this team convention prefers procedures unannotated
8:1-8:14 info visibility_annotation_usage: Visibility annotation '/*@protected;' - this team convention prefers procedures unannotated
